#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265970 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105826 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce428740-1268-5071-9a45-69cdc07aea64" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Probability of a Binomial Random Variable Over an Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19893c26-ed3a-5413-afc2-a0d8f99cb004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.329" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263243} {:answer/id #uuid "2b7845b2-eff1-53f6-ac81-13b44ac66e24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.296" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263368} {:answer/id #uuid "30a8d306-0d26-54c5-9bcb-4815f9dcbe4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.407" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263414} {:answer/id #uuid "9c845a96-9529-5da5-883a-d69c35a7093e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.156" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264340} {:answer/id #uuid "b8934eb6-83b1-5f57-b0a7-224ad71b202b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.889" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264595}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30a8d306-0d26-54c5-9bcb-4815f9dcbe4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.407" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263414} :answer-field/id #uuid "eac393bd-fb71-5e07-86e1-307bf6913530" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265663}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d0bf184d-d7ca-56cb-ba56-14f65e4f1f16" :question/math-academy-id "q-130746" :question/problem "A box of chocolates contains cherry creams and almond little cakes in the ratio of $2:1.$ Four chocolates are selected at random, with replacement. What is the probability of getting at most $2$ cherry creams? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be the number of selected cherry creams.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=4$ selected chocolates\n\n- since cherry creams and almond little cakes are in the ratio of $2:1,$ the probability of selecting a cherry cream from the box is $p=\\frac{2}{3}$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(4,\\frac{2}{3}).$ \n\nThe number of successes of a binomial random variable has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nP(X=x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSubstituting the above information into the formula for probability mass function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{x}){(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x}{(1-\\frac{2}{3})}^{4-x} \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{x}){(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{4-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to find the probability of getting at most $2$ cherry creams. So, we compute\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2) & =P(X=0)+P(X=1)+P(X=2) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{0}){(\\frac{2}{3})}^{0}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{4-0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{1}){(\\frac{2}{3})}^{1}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{4-1}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{2}){(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{4-2} \\\\  & =1{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{0}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{4}+4{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{1}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{3}+6{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & ≈0.407\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}]}
